        <type><ref refid="classONNX__LIGHT__NAMESPACE_1_1TensorProto" kindref="compound">TensorProto</ref></type>
        <definition>TensorProto ONNX_LIGHT_NAMESPACE::SparseTensorProto::indices</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>indices</name>
        <qualifiedname>ONNX_LIGHT_NAMESPACE::SparseTensorProto::indices</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>&quot;The indices of the non-default values, which may be stored in one of two formats. (a) &quot; &quot;Indices can be a tensor of shape [NNZ, rank] with the [i,j]-th value corresponding to &quot; &quot;the j-th index of the i-th value (in the values tensor). (b) Indices can be a tensor of &quot; &quot;shape [NNZ], in which case the i-th value must be the linearized-index of the i-th &quot; &quot;value (in the values tensor). The linearized-index can be converted into an index tuple &quot; &quot;(k_1,...,k_rank) using the shape provided below. The indices must appear in ascending &quot; &quot;order without duplication. In the first format, the ordering is lexicographic-ordering: &quot; &quot;e.g., index-value [1,4] must appear before [2,1].&quot; <linebreak/>
 </para>
        </detaileddescription>
